## 3. Project Title

Exploratory Data Analysis of Supermarket Sales Using Pandas

This project focuses on analyzing supermarket sales data to understand sales performance, customer purchasing behavior, product category performance, and customer satisfaction. Python and Pandas will be used to prepare, analyze, and summarize the dataset.

## 4. Dataset Information

Dataset Title: Supermarket Sales Dataset

Source Website / URL:

https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/aungpyaeap/supermarket-sales

An accessible copy of the dataset is also available here:

https://github.com/SarahShafqat/Kaggle-Datasets/blob/master/supermarket_sales.csv

Description of the dataset:

The Supermarket Sales Dataset contains historical sales transactions from three supermarket branches in Myanmar. The records cover January to March 2019.

The dataset includes information about invoices, branch locations, customer types, gender, product categories, unit prices, quantities purchased, taxes, total sales, payment methods, gross income, and customer ratings.

The dataset contains 1,000 sales records and 17 columns. It provides both numerical and categorical data, making it useful for exploratory data analysis.

Why this dataset was selected:

The dataset was selected because it is publicly available, understandable, and suitable for beginner-level data analysis. It contains different types of information that can be analyzed using Pandas.

The dataset allows the team to practice data cleaning, filtering, sorting, grouping, aggregation, pivot tables, and visualization. It also helps demonstrate how data analysis can support business decisions.

Size of dataset:

- Rows: 1,000 sales transactions
- Columns: 17 variables
- Period covered: January–March 2019
- Locations: Three supermarket branches in Myanmar

The 1,000 rows refer to data records, excluding the header row in the CSV file.

## 5. Project Objectives

### What problem are you trying to solve?

Businesses collect large amounts of sales data, but the data is not always easy to understand without analysis. Managers need to know which products perform well, which locations generate more revenue, how customers pay, and whether customers are satisfied.

The purpose of this project is to analyze supermarket sales data and turn it into useful information that can support business decisions.

### What questions do you want to answer using data analysis?

1. Which product categories generate the highest total sales?
2. Which supermarket branch or city generates the most revenue?
3. Which payment method is used most frequently?
4. What is the average transaction value?
5. How many products are purchased per transaction on average?
6. Which customer type generates more sales: members or normal customers?
7. What is the average customer rating?
